Purpose: Do not load system-wide or per-user external extension directories on Linux (/usr/share/chromium/extensions/*.json auto-installs from, and updates against, the Chrome Web Store without user action; seen on the dev host with the GNOME Shell integration). Extensions come from the preinstalled provider (0320) or the user.
Area: debrand
Files: chrome/browser/extensions/external_provider_impl.cc
Rebase risk: medium because it removes a block inside CreateExternalProviders, which is edited regularly
Origin: original (written for Corvid; no third-party patch text reused)

